---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is Ultimate Frisbee? | Flyght Ultimate Nottingham"
  description="Ultimate is a fast-paced, non-contact, self-refereed team sport played with a flying disc. Learn the basics and the Spirit of the Game, then try it with Flyght in Nottingham."
>
  <section class="page container">
    <h1>What is Ultimate Frisbee?</h1>
    <p>
      Ultimate is a fast-paced, non-contact, self-refereed team sport played with a flying disc (frisbee). The goal is to
      score points by catching the disc in the opposing team's end zone.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is played by two teams of seven players on a rectangular field with end zones at each end. Players advance the disc
      by passing it to teammates. The defending team can intercept the disc or force a turnover by causing the disc to touch
      the ground. The game emphasizes sportsmanship and fair play, with players responsible for their own calls and disputes
      resolved through discussion.
    </p>

    <h2>Spirit of the Game</h2>
    <p>
      Ultimate relies upon a Spirit of the Game that places the responsibility for fair play on every player. There are
      no referees; the players are solely responsible for following and enforcing the rules, even at World Championship.
      Competitive play is encouraged, but never at the expense of respect between players, adherence to the rules, and the
      basic joy of play.
    </p>

    <div class="video-embed responsive-embed">
      <iframe
        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/hXArTyZcjPA?start=138"
        title="Introduction to ultimate frisbee (YouTube video)"
        loading="lazy"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
        allowfullscreen
      ></iframe>
    </div>

    <h2>Play ultimate in Nottingham</h2>
    <p>
      Flyght welcomes players of all skill levels, from absolute beginners to experienced players. Check
      <a href="/#where-do-we-train">where and when we train</a> or <a href="/contact/">send us a message</a> and we'll be
      more than happy to help.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
